 "intro": "By the river Muthul in Numidia, 109 BC. You are the consul Quintus Caecilius Metellus, sent after the disgrace at Suthul. Your legates include Gaius Marius and Publius Rutilius Rufus.",
 "debrief": "In Sallust’s account, Metellus restored discipline, then marched across a bare plain toward the Muthul with Rutilius sent ahead to make camp by the river. Jugurtha’s horsemen attacked from the scrub on a ridge; the Romans fought all afternoon in small groups, and Marius took a hill the Numidians were using. At the river, Rutilius beat Bomilcar’s infantry and took the elephants. Jugurtha’s army was scattered, but he escaped, and the war went on until 105 BC. The other choices are what-ifs.",
